        return v
```

A few best practices apply across both versions. Always return the value (or values) from a validator, because forgetting to do so leads to missing or incorrect data. Use `before` mode for transformation and `after` mode for validation of the built model, and avoid duplicating logic between the two. Prefer the V2 decorators (`@field_validator`, `@model_validator`) for new code, since `@validator` and `@root_validator` are legacy.

